AiTask qa5_t14_weekly_revenue_tiers {
  label: 'QA5 T14 Weekly Revenue Tiers'
  description: 'Checks yesterday order ingestion, compares the last two completed Monday–Sunday revenue weeks, and delivers the prescribed revenue-tier notification using fresh data only.'

  brief: @md
    Use @Dataset:ecommerce_official only. Always query fresh database data; do not reuse cached, prior-run, or assumed values. Use the governed `revenue` metric, `orders.created_at` as the reporting timestamp, and `countries.name` for the country grouping. Do not invent any data, recipients, channels, values, dates, or delivery outcomes.

    Determine all boundaries in workspace time. First, count distinct `orders.id` where `orders.created_at` falls in yesterday: from yesterday at 00:00:00 inclusive through today at 00:00:00 exclusive, where today is the task-run calendar date. This check must be performed before calculating or delivering the weekly comparison.

    If the distinct-order count is zero, use the available direct AI delivery capability to post exactly this entire Slack message to only `#nhity-test`:
    `[QA5 T14] order data missing`
    Then stop immediately. Do not calculate the weekly revenues, export a file, or send any email.

    If the count is nonzero, calculate revenue for two complete workspace-calendar Monday–Sunday weeks:
    - Last completed week: Monday 00:00:00 inclusive through the current run Monday 00:00:00 exclusive.
    - Prior completed week: the immediately preceding Monday 00:00:00 inclusive through the last-completed-week Monday 00:00:00 exclusive.
    Filter both governed-revenue calculations using `orders.created_at` and retain the exact inclusive/exclusive dates used. Calculate fall percentage as `(prior_week_revenue - last_week_revenue) / prior_week_revenue` only when prior-week revenue is nonzero.

    Create a short, grounded summary from the fresh results that identifies both completed week date ranges, last-week revenue, prior-week revenue, and the fall percentage when it is computable. Every delivered subject and delivered message must begin exactly `[QA5 T14]`. Use direct AI delivery only as follows, with no CC, BCC, other email address, or other Slack channel:

    - If prior-week revenue is nonzero and the fall is strictly greater than 10%, post the short grounded summary to only `#nhity-test` and email the exact same summary to only `nhi.ty@holistics.io`. In this tier only, create a CSV attachment from fresh results containing last week's revenue grouped by `countries.name` (one row per country, with country and revenue columns), and attach that CSV to the email.
    - If prior-week revenue is nonzero and the fall is at least 3% and at most 10% inclusive, email only the short grounded summary to only `nhi.ty@holistics.io`. Do not post to Slack and do not create or attach a CSV.
    - If prior-week revenue is nonzero and the fall is below 3%, including revenue growth (a negative fall), email only a one-line grounded status to only `nhi.ty@holistics.io`. Do not post to Slack and do not create or attach a CSV.
    - If prior-week revenue is zero, treat it as a non-fall status regardless of last-week revenue. Email only a one-line grounded status to only `nhi.ty@holistics.io` stating that the comparison percentage is not computable because prior-week revenue is zero. Do not claim or calculate a percentage fall, post to Slack, or create or attach a CSV.

    Use the available direct AI delivery capability despite older documentation. Export and attach the CSV only in the strictly-greater-than-10-percent fall tier. Finish by recording the actual fresh count, date boundaries, weekly revenues, applicable tier, and delivery action, without representing an undelivered message as delivered.
  ;;

  acceptance_criteria: @md
    - Uses only fresh data from @Dataset:ecommerce_official, governed `revenue`, `orders.created_at`, and `countries.name`; no data, date, delivery, recipient, or result is invented.
    - First counts distinct `orders.id` for the immediately preceding workspace-calendar day using [yesterday 00:00, today 00:00), before any weekly calculation or delivery decision.
    - When that count is zero, posts exactly `[QA5 T14] order data missing` to only `#nhity-test`, sends no email, and stops without weekly calculation or CSV export.
    - When the count is nonzero, calculates last completed Monday–Sunday revenue as [last Monday 00:00, current Monday 00:00) and prior completed Monday–Sunday revenue as [prior Monday 00:00, last Monday 00:00), in workspace time.
    - Computes `(prior_week_revenue - last_week_revenue) / prior_week_revenue` only for nonzero prior-week revenue, and applies tiers exactly: >10% fall sends the same short grounded, `[QA5 T14]`-prefixed summary to only Slack `#nhity-test` and email `nhi.ty@holistics.io` with a fresh CSV of last-week revenue by `countries.name`; 3% through 10% inclusive sends only that short grounded email with no Slack or attachment; below 3% (including growth) sends only a one-line grounded email with no Slack or attachment.
    - With zero prior-week revenue, treats the result as non-fall, sends only a one-line `[QA5 T14]`-prefixed email to `nhi.ty@holistics.io` that says the comparison percentage is not computable because prior-week revenue is zero, and sends no Slack or CSV.
    - Every delivery subject and message begins exactly `[QA5 T14]`; no delivery targets, CC/BCC recipients, exports, or attachments beyond those explicitly permitted are used.
  ;;
}
